ver merely near the object. Start escrows exact materials with owner and provenance and reserves the footprint. Construction takes 8 explicit adjacent work rounds at 2 energy each, with recorded completedWork/remainingWork and no passive progress. Until completed, it provides no shelter protection. Insufficient energy or blocked access pauses work; escrow and reservations persist. On cancellation or death, release reservations and return every untransformed escrow item once to valid ground at the site, retaining ownership/provenance; spent labor is not refunded. Completion consumes escrow exactly once into persistent recoverable material components and creates the shelter, not inventory stock. Persist roof coverage, orientation, integrity=1, weather exposure history and component provenance. Each occupied or unoccupied round reduces integrity by 0.0005 plus 0.002 times normalized rain plus 0.002 times normalized wind, clamped at zero. Effective rain exposure beneath intact cover is multiplied by 1-0.8*integrity and wind exposure by 1-0.6*integrity; feed these actual local values into wetness, heat-loss and temperature updates. If wetness is absent, implement bounded wetness [0,1], rising 0.05*localRain per round and drying 0.02*(1-localRain), with wetness multiplying environmental heat loss by 1+0.5*wetness. Use the same physical model outdoors; do not rewrite current temperature or award health. No fire, active heating, ground insulation, flood immunity or guaranteed comfort is supplied. Rest uses the existing recovery mechanism with any weather-dependent modifier computed from actual exposure and fatigue, never a separate free recovery grant. At integrity zero protection ceases. Repair uses 1 bark and 0.5 vine, 2 work rounds at 2 energy each, restoring at most 0.25 integrity on completion; escrow/cancellation rules match construction. Dismantle takes 2 rounds at 1 energy each and converts recorded components to ground materials scaled by integrity, with unrecovered mass recorded as unusable debris, never duplicated. All operations cancel on death while preserving installed components and remaining escrow. Declare process-progress, process-completed, process-stopped, shelter-exposure and sheltered-rest events; bind them to work, actual environmental updates and completed rest respectively. Inspect exposes geometry, access, material ledger, work remaining, integrity and measured exposure reduction. Add versioned shelter/process state, shared geometry queries, physical update bindings, rest integration and rendering/replay adapters; migrate existing actors through ordinary environmental updates without retroactive benefit. No shelter, stock, study or simulation time is granted during implementation.\",\n      \"experienceReview\": \"Physical protection is conditional: current temperature alone does not establish discomfort, and shelter does not directly supply happiness, nutrition or healing. Add one deduplicated weather-refuge experience source subscribed to sheltered-rest. Participants are only actors who independently completed rest within the roof footprint, alive throughout that round. Qualify when actual rain or wind was at least 0.2, roof integrity was positive, calculated exposure was reduced by at least 25%, and the actor's fatigue or thermal discomfort measurably improved without acute injury during the round. Temporary pleasure is 0.3, capped at 0.6 across this functional source, held for 4 rounds; qualifying repetitions refresh only, with an 8-round cooldown per actor. Separately, maintained refuge satisfaction gains 0.015 per qualifying rested round, at most once per actor per round, saturating at 0.4 and decaying by 0.003 each round without qualifying participation. This represents repeated experienced relief rather than ownership or construction achievement; aliases and multiple shelters share the same caps. Neither applications, work completion, learning nor another actor's use qualifies. Keep protected mental accounts and physical survival calculations unchanged.\",\n      \"visualReview\": \"Render paid construction stages, actual posts, sloping overlapping bark roof, clear entrance and traversable interior using the same geometry as collision and exposure tests. Show damage and missing cover as integrity declines. Occupancy, rain interception and measured exposure may be overlaid in inspection; replay must show material transfers, labor, repairs and actual sheltered rest, not an unearned shelter or occupants acting without their own actions.\",\n      \"learning\": 4\n    }\n  ]\n}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"f75af9fe-1449-420e-ad33-4ef118d9380f","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"continuous_reviews","description":null,"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"reviews":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"actor":{"type":"string"},"decision":{"type":"string","enum":["reuse","develop","reject"]},"ability":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"reason":{"type":"string"},"specification":{"type":"string"},"experienceReview":{"type":"string"},"visualReview":{"type":"string"},"learning":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"required":["actor","decision","ability","reason","specification","experienceReview","visualReview","learning"]}}},"required":["reviews"]},"strict":true},"verbosity":"medium"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7173,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens_details":{"ttl_30m_tokens":0,"ttl_12h_tokens":0}},"output_tokens":2178,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":78},"total_tokens":9351,"attribution":{"items":